    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-106487",
      "summary": "### Impact\n\nDeployments using catalog cluster discovery may be affected when catalog contributors can create or modify `kubernetes-cluster` Resource entities. With the required endpoint permissions and pod RBAC, the backend can use its local in-cluster identity, potentially exposing Kubernetes resources readable by that identity. The credential is used only with the local in-cluster API endpoint and is not sent to the catalog-supplied endpoint.\n\n### Patches\n\nPatched in `@backstage/plugin-kubernetes-backend` version `0.21.10`\n\n### Workarounds\n\n- Do not configure service account authentication through catalog-provided clusters; use the supported static configuration method when service account authentication is required.\n- Restrict catalog ingestion so untrusted users cannot create or alter Kubernetes cluster Resource entities.",
      "cvssScore": 3.5,
      "severity": "Low",
      "published": "2026-10-07",
      "modified": "2026-10-07",
      "cwe": {
        "cwe_id": "CWE-441",
        "name": "Unintended Proxy or Intermediary ('Confused Deputy')"
      },
      "references": [
        "https://github.com/backstage/backstage/security/advisories/GHSA-h53x-hjx6-25gr",
        "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-106487",
        "https://github.com/backstage/backstage/commit/c14f8be6908f0f719b16356e5492352311e28946",
        "https://github.com/backstage/backstage/releases/tag/v1.54.6",
        "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-h53x-hjx6-25gr"
      ],
      "vulnerableProducts": [
        "@backstage/plugin-kubernetes-backend npm"
      ],
      "isExploited": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-106488",
      "summary": "### Impact\n\nDeployments using OIDC email-based identity resolution with a provider that permits unverified email addresses may allow an authenticated provider user to assume another catalog identity. This may grant access and permissions associated with that user. No direct availability impact is demonstrated.\n\n### Patches\n\nPatched in `@backstage/plugin-auth-backend-module-oidc-provider` version `0.4.20`.\n\n### Workarounds\n\n- Disable email-based sign-in resolution for the OIDC provider, or require the identity provider to verify email addresses before allowing sign-in.",
      "cvssScore": 8.1,
      "severity": "High",
      "published": "2026-10-07",
      "modified": "2026-10-07",
